          {
            "label": "Ask your history a question",
            "sections": [
              {
                "heading": "Ask your history a question",
                "accent": "cyan",
                "text": [ "Natural-language AI history search." ],
                "bullets": [
                  "The owner types \"did the dog walker come yesterday?\" and **Halogate** authenticates and routes the question to **Concierge**.",
                  "**Concierge**'s LLM parses the question into a structured query: range = yesterday, subject = person + dog, cameras = all non-E2EE.",
                  "**Concierge** sends the structured query to **Chronicle**, which runs it against labels and embeddings.",
                  "**Chronicle** returns the top matches with descriptions and thumbnails, marking E2EE cameras \"unsearchable\" rather than silently omitting them.",
                  "**Concierge** composes the answer (\"Yes — 2:14 pm, front yard, 4 minutes\") and returns it through **Halogate** to the phone.",
                  "The owner taps a result and the app streams the matched clip from **Vault**.",
                  "**Lens AI down** — plain \"motion detected\" pushes; Chronicle re-indexes from the backlog on recovery, so search has a blind window, not a hole."
                ],
                "diagram": {
                  "view": "ambient",
