          {
            "label": "Virtual guard — a human takes over",
            "sections": [
              {
                "heading": "Virtual guard — a human takes over",
                "accent": "amber",
                "text": [ "The human virtual-guard session." ],
                "bullets": [
                  "A person lingers in the driveway after midnight and the camera streams the event to **Conduit**.",
                  "**Conduit** forwards frames to **Lens AI**, which classifies a person at 0.94 confidence loitering 38 seconds.",
                  "**Lens AI** posts a guard-eligible alert to **Watchtower**, which confirms the home's Guard entitlement with **Ledger**.",
                  "**Watchtower** opens incident CB-8841 in **Casebook** and assigns it to the next free agent at **Agent Desk**.",
                  "**Agent Desk** opens a live WebRTC view of the camera through **Conduit**; the agent sees the scene in under five seconds.",
                  "The agent triggers the talk-down and **Agent Desk** routes their audio through **Conduit** to the camera speaker.",
                  "The subject stays, so the agent escalates and **Conduit** relays the siren command; the camera sounds 105 dB.",
                  "The subject leaves the frame; the agent marks the outcome \"deterred\" and **Agent Desk** writes the resolution to **Casebook**.",
                  "**Casebook** hands the finished incident to **Clarion**, which pushes the summary and audit link to the owner.",
                  "**Wifi drops** — no offline buffer by design (thin-camera model): events in the gap are lost, and history shows an honest \"camera offline\" span.",
                  "**Battery low (Doorbell)** — below 15% Iris wake is rationed to radar hits under 3 m; below 5% Ward logs motion timestamps only.",
                  "**Watchtower saturated** — incidents past the 60 s claim SLA degrade to a rich notification with a one-tap siren shortcut; the miss is recorded."
                ],
                "contract": {
                  "title": "On the wire: event envelope (camera → Conduit)",
                  "source": "https://github.com/halovista/firmware/blob/main/halo/iris/envelope.c#L142",
                  "fields": [
                    { "k": "event_id", "v": "\"ev_7c31a9\"", "g": "camera-minted id; dedup key everywhere downstream" },
                    { "k": "camera_id", "v": "\"halo-4f22\"", "g": "device identity from the HV-SE1 cert" },
                    { "k": "ts", "v": "1757085660", "g": "wall-clock seconds at trigger" },
                    { "k": "class", "v": "\"person\"", "g": "Ward/Iris local pre-classification hint" },
                    { "k": "radar_m", "v": "4.2", "g": "radar distance at trigger, meters" },
                    { "k": "e2ee", "v": "false", "g": "true = payload is ciphertext; Lens AI must skip", "hot": true },
                    { "k": "media", "v": "\"vault://halo-4f22/ev_7c31a9\"", "g": "clip object reference" }
                  ]
                },
                "diagram": {
                  "view": "ambient",
                  "nodes": {
                    "cam": { "title": "Halo Cam", "sub": "driveway", "icon": "chip", "tint": "dev" },
                    "conduit": { "title": "Conduit", "sub": "device broker", "icon": "antenna", "tint": "mqtt",
                      "link": "https://github.com/halovista/platform/blob/main/services/conduit/broker.go#L64" },
